/* book: lead: An open thin-walled section, an angle, channel, Z or stringer, has no closed loop for a shear flow to circulate round. It carries torque the way a flat strip does, with shear stress that changes sign through the thickness. Its torsion constant grows with the cube of the wall thickness, so it is very flexible in torsion. This chapter gives J = Σbt³/3, the surface stress and the rate of twist, and c */
