/* book Worked example: Q: A 2 mm strip 120 mm long is formed (a) into an equal angle with 60 mm legs and (b) into a closed square tube of 30 mm side. Each is 1 m long, aluminium with G = 27 GPa, and carries T = 10 N·m. Find J, the largest shear stress and the twist for each.
   1. (a) J = (60 × 2³ + 60 × 2³)/3 = 960/3 = 320 mm⁴.
   2. τmax = T t/J = 10,000 × 2/320 = 62.5 N/mm², on the faces of both legs.
   3. dθ/dz = T/GJ = 10,000/(27,000 × 320) = 1.157 × 10⁻³ rad/mm; over 1 m θ = 1.157 rad = 66.3°.
   4. (b) A = 30 × 30 = 900 mm², ∮ds/t = 120/2 = 60, J = 4 × 900²/60 = 54,000 mm⁴.
   5. q = T/2A = 10,000/1800 = 5.56 N/mm; τ = q/t = 2.78 N/mm².
   6. θ = 10,000 × 1000/(27,000 × 54,000) = 0.00686 rad = 0.393°.
   7. Ratio of stiffness: 54,000/320 = 169; ratio of stress: 62.5/2.78 = 22.5.
   Answer: Angle: J = 320 mm⁴, τmax = 62.5 N/mm², θ = 66.3°. Tube: J = 54,000 mm⁴, τ = 2.78 N/mm², θ = 0.393°. Same strip, 169 times stiffer when closed. */
