/* book Worked example 2: Q: A channel stringer has two flanges 50 mm × 3 mm and a web 100 mm × 2 mm (mid-line lengths). It carries T = 15 N·m, with G = 27 GPa. Find J, the stress in the flanges and in the web, and the rate of twist.
   1. J = (2 × 50 × 3³ + 100 × 2³)/3 = (2700 + 800)/3 = 1166.7 mm⁴.
   2. Rate of twist: T/GJ = 15,000/(27,000 × 1166.7) = 4.762 × 10⁻⁴ rad/mm = 0.476 rad/m (27.3° per metre).
   3. Flange faces: τ = T t/J = 15,000 × 3/1166.7 = 38.6 N/mm².
   4. Web faces: τ = 15,000 × 2/1166.7 = 25.7 N/mm².
   5. The flanges, two-thirds of the wall length, provide 77 per cent of J because of the cube of their thickness.
   Answer: J = 1166.7 mm⁴; τ = 38.6 N/mm² in the flanges and 25.7 N/mm² in the web; 27.3° per metre. */
